# Expander

A prominent disclosure can divide an overwhelming reference topic into manageable sections.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for substantial help that a broad audience may need, after testing a shorter page with ordinary headings. It is more prominent than a small details disclosure.

## When not to use it

Do not put expanders around live device controls, form questions, critical alerts or the only explanation of a failed action. Avoid nesting them inside other disclosures.

## Home Assistant adaptation

For Home Assistant help, expanders may organise explanations of recorded Energy values or dashboard visibility. They are a reference-content pattern, not a new container for every card. Preserve the user’s open sections when unrelated readings change.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use semantic details and summary with clear text, a visible focus treatment and a programmatically exposed expanded state. Multiple sections can remain open for comparison. Keep the summary free of separate interactive controls.

